1. DEFINITIONS

"SDK" means the software in this package (the files in src/ and anything this license
accompanies), including the copy served at https://forevermachines.net/sdk/.

"Materials" means the machines, effects, the kit, the skins (themes) and any other code or
data that the SDK loads, or that is served from forevermachines.net under /kit, /machines,
/effects, /sleep and /sdk, whether or not through the SDK.

"Application" means an app, website, game, device or service that you build and that uses
the SDK or the Materials.

"Output" means the sound produced, and the pictures drawn, when the Materials run in
your Application.

"You" means the person or organization using the SDK or the Materials. "We" and "us" mean
Juan Maguid, trading as Temperamento (the Licensor).

2. FREE USE

You may, without charge, use, run, copy and modify the SDK and the Materials:

(a) to evaluate them, and to develop and test an Application that is not yet offered to others;
(b) in personal projects that are not offered for sale or used to earn money, directly or
    indirectly (including by advertising, subscriptions, in-app purchases or paid access);
(c) for teaching, study and research that is not commercial.

When you use the Materials under this section in anything shown to others, keep a visible
credit such as "Sound by Forever Machines" with a link to https://forevermachines.net.

3. COMMERCIAL USE

Any other use needs a commercial license from us, agreed in writing (an order form, an
invoice that says so, or a signed agreement), with the price, term, number of Applications and
any support or key terms set out there. In particular, you need one before you make an
Application available to users who are not you, if you or your organization earn money from it
or it is part of a business. Until you have one, Section 2 is all you may do. A commercial
license may also include API keys: using the Materials without a key where one is required is
not licensed.

4. WHAT YOU MAY DO WITH A LICENSE (free or commercial)

Subject to Section 2 or 3 and to this license as a whole, you get a worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable right to:

(a) embed the SDK and run the Materials unmodified in your Application;
(b) modify the SDK's source as needed to integrate it, for your own Application only, keeping
    these notices;
(c) let the end users of your Application hear and see the Output.

5. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

(a) Resell, rent, sublicense, publish or redistribute the SDK or the Materials, in whole or in
    part, as a product, library, package, API, template or collection, or bundle them in an
    offering whose value is mainly them.
(b) Copy, scrape or extract machines, effects or the kit to build or populate a competing
    collection, marketplace, library or service.
(c) Sell or distribute recordings of the Output as standalone audio (sample packs, stock audio,
    loops, music libraries), or register it with a collecting society or a content-ID system as
    your own work.
(d) Use the Materials, or what they produce, to train, fine-tune or evaluate a machine-learning
    model, or to build a dataset for that purpose.
(e) Remove, hide or change copyright, license or credit notices.
(f) Bypass any key, rate limit or access control, or load the Materials from our servers in a way
    that puts an unreasonable load on them.
(g) Use the SDK or the Materials for anything unlawful, or to build malware or to harm others.

